    "done_when": "Named ids: tests/test_a_discard_never_reads_promoted.py::test_a_discarded_block_never_reads_promoted and tests/test_crew_discard_reads_discarded.py::test_a_discard_leaves_no_record_when_its_run_directory_is_gone, both red since 5bd8460fb moved the classification memo into each run's own run directory as classification.json. A classification read now creates the run directory, so a discard finds a directory to mark and rmdir finds it non-empty. For each id, the node first decides whether the test pins a fixture the shipped rule makes stale, or the shipped change is wrong. It names the decision and its evidence in the landing record. A stale fixture is moved to the shipped rule. A product defect is repaired in the named product file only when it is inside this node's write paths; otherwise it goes to follow_ons with file:line. No test is skipped, xfailed, deleted or weakened. A read that creates state is the likely defect: the memo should not be written for a run whose directory does not exist. A new case asserts that classify_pointer over a pointer with no run directory leaves none behind. Base and head arms of those two files, tests/test_pointer_classification_is_memoised.py and tests/test_a_live_run_never_reads_dead.py show zero added failures.",
